adjudication.rationale:
In `SpanFlusher.join()`, the new loop over `self.processes` breaks out entirely when `remaining_time <= 0` (deadline exceeded):
```py
for process_index, process in self.processes.items():
    if deadline is not None:
        remaining_time = deadline - time.time()
        if remaining_time <= 0:
            break
    ...
    if isinstance(process, multiprocessing.Process):
        process.terminate()
```
That `break` prevents visiting/terminating any remaining processes, so they may continue running after `join(timeout=...)` returns (i.e., potential orphaned flusher processes). This behavior is introduced by the rewritten multi-process join logic.
